{
  "summary": "Clarifies in the `addnode` RPC help text that `MAX_ADDNODE_CONNECTIONS` only limits persistent `add` connections and does not apply to `onetry` attempts. In `bitcoin-cli -netinfo`, expands the manual peer count tracker from `uint8_t` to `uint16_t` to match other counters and avoid integer overflow.",
  "problem": "The `addnode` RPC documentation states a connection limit without clarifying that it only applies to persistent additions, misleading users about `onetry` behaviour. Furthermore, because `onetry` connections can accumulate beyond 255 manual peers, `-netinfo`'s `uint8_t` counter wraps at 256, displaying incorrect counts or causing the column to vanish.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit 77410ed3b7: 'The other -netinfo peer counts are uint16_t, but the manual peer count was uint8_t and wraps at 256. Manual peers aren't limited to the 8 -addnode slots (addnode onetry connections also count as manual and are not subject to MAX_ADDNODE_CONNECTIONS), so the count can reach that and the \"manual\" column then disappears or shows a wrapped value.'"
